</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, MASANORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAOKA, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A sheet hot rolling mill, wherein its finishing rolling mill (30) is divided into front and rear stages (31 and 32), and CVC mills (31A and 31B) of two stands or more are disposed on the front stage (31) and different diameter roll mills (32A and 32B) of two stands or more are disposed on the rear stage (32), whereby, when a thin sheet about 1.2 mm thick or thinner is rolled, a crown or edge drop is suppressed from occurring and also a drawing is prevented from occurring at the tail end part of the sheet so that a rolled sheet can be manufactured smoothly.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un laminoir à bandes à chaud, dans lequel le train finisseur (30) est divisé en étages avant (31) et arrière (32), l'étage avant (31) comprenant deux ou plusieurs cages de rouleaux CVC (31A et 31B) et l'étage arrière (32) comprenant deux ou plusieurs cages (32A et 32B) contenant des rouleaux de travail de diamètres différents. Lorsqu'une bande d'environ 1,2 mm d'épaisseur, ou plus fine, est laminée, le train finisseur de l'invention permet d'éviter le bombement ou l'amincissement d'extrémité ainsi qu'un étirement sur la partie terminale de la bande, ce qui permet d'obtenir une bande laminée plane.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms